    <statement><p>Solve for the unknown variable.</p>
<p><m>\ln (x^{10}) - \ln (x^{4}) = 6</m></p>
<p><m>x =</m>  <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2.71828</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\ln(x^{10})-\ln(x^{4})=\ln ( \frac{x^{10}}{x^{4}} )=\ln (x^{6})= 6 \ln x</m>. Thus, <m>6 \ln x =6</m> or <m>\ln x =1</m>.  


 Hence, <m>x=e</m>.






</solution>
